1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,000
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,320
=Episode 8=

4
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:51,600
(Physician)
Help me!

5
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:52,359
Miss!

6
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:54,119
What happened?

7
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:55,560
I was bitten while I was out.

8
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,880
Miss, you've been poisoned
by snake venom.

9
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,359
I need to drain

10
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,520
the tainted blood right away.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,840
This may hurt.

12
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,000
Try to bear with it.

13
00:01:12,519 --> 00:01:14,400
Take these medicines as directed.

14
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:14,840
All right.

15
00:01:15,439 --> 00:01:16,319
Thank you, Ms. Xiaoqing.

16
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,000
Can you stand?

17
00:01:20,959 --> 00:01:22,000
I've drained the tainted blood.

18
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,079
If you'd come an hour later,

19
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:25,560
you would've lost this arm.

20
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,560
Thank you, miss.

21
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:28,359
Mr. Gu.

22
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,799
Get the pain-relief powder.

23
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:30,280
All right.

24
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:33,640
Here.

25
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,599
Thank you.

26
00:01:38,359 --> 00:01:39,040
Your Maj...

27
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:46,159
Thank you, sir.

28
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:47,879
Avoid meat and fish for a few days.

29
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,560
Change the dressing once a day.

30
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,120
All right.

31
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:53,000
I'll send someone by later

32
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,040
with the fee.

33
00:01:54,799 --> 00:01:55,519
I'll take my leave.

34
00:02:05,719 --> 00:02:06,719
We're out of firewood.

35
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,120
I'll go get some.

36
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:09,599
All right.

37
00:02:21,039 --> 00:02:22,000
Please spare my life!

38
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,639
I swear I won't tell anyone

39
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:24,560
who you really are.

40
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,520
Don't kill me!

41
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,840
I like that I'm just Mr. Gu to her.

42
00:02:47,879 --> 00:02:50,000
No one gets to ruin that.

43
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,159
Take her back
to Minister Liu's residence.

44
00:02:53,479 --> 00:02:54,520
Tell Minister Liu

45
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:55,879
his daughter was killed

46
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:56,879
by bandits on her way home.

47
00:02:57,479 --> 00:02:59,280
I'll have the Capital Prefecture
investigate thoroughly.

48
00:03:00,039 --> 00:03:00,439
Yes.

49
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:06,800
Done.

50
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:15,639
Hold this.

51
00:03:19,759 --> 00:03:20,400
See?

52
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,240
This part...

53
00:03:24,759 --> 00:03:26,360
goes around the back.

54
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,199
Didn't you do that yourself?

55
00:03:28,199 --> 00:03:30,000
♪Peach blossoms fill your window again♪

56
00:03:30,759 --> 00:03:31,800
There. I've got it now.

57
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,759
You've got it?

58
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,439
You're hopeless.

59
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Why can't you get it?

60
00:03:37,639 --> 00:03:38,680
It looks good to me.

61
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:40,800
And you're laughing?

62
00:03:41,039 --> 00:03:41,840
Look at what you made.

63
00:03:42,039 --> 00:03:42,599
What's this?

64
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:43,919
What even is this?

65
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:45,960
Still laughing at me?

66
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:48,360
Run! Run!

67
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:50,919
You still dare laugh at me?

68
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,800
♪A quiet sigh♪

69
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:58,680
♪Longing hides hope between the lines♪

70
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,560
♪A ray of spring brings warmth♪

71
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,400
♪A tree bursts into bloom♪

72
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,360
♪Across hills and rivers, I await you♪

73
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,200
♪Borrow half a city's warmth♪

74
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,160
♪For half a lifetime of love♪

75
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,120
♪May we have a lifetime of peace♪

76
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,960
♪I only wish you'd stay with me forever♪

77
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,880
♪A ray of spring brings warmth♪

78
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,720
♪A tree bursts into bloom♪

79
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,680
♪Across hills and rivers, I await you♪

80
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,560
♪Sharing the warmth of spring♪

81
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,480
♪May half a lifetime's wish come true♪

82
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,360
♪Borrow a whole city's warmth♪

83
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:29,240
♪I only wish your heart were like mine♪

84
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,320
♪Side by side♪

85
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,600
I heard Guizhen Cottage

86
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,879
was built by His Majesty

87
00:04:35,079 --> 00:04:36,399
for the late Empress.

88
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,000
What do you think

89
00:04:39,639 --> 00:04:41,720
of the cottage?

90
00:04:42,319 --> 00:04:44,399
It may look simple,

91
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,680
but I hear more went into it

92
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,160
than even a palace.

93
00:04:48,279 --> 00:04:50,720
Yet so many people go hungry.

94
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:54,040
Why build on such a grand scale

95
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,639
for someone who's already gone?

96
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:00,519
That's what I thought at first.

97
00:05:01,199 --> 00:05:01,959
But later,

98
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,560
I heard the elders nearby

99
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,879
often tell stories about

100
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,839
His Majesty and the late Empress,

101
00:05:07,439 --> 00:05:08,399
and I changed my mind.

102
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:10,240
This isn't extravagance.

103
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,680
It's devotion.

104
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,759
So much in this world

105
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,160
fades away.

106
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:16,839
Reputation.

107
00:05:17,639 --> 00:05:18,360
Glory.

108
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,439
Even true feelings can fade.

109
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:22,600
To find someone

110
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,959
who cares for you that sincerely

111
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,040
is truly rare.

112
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,600
♪If I could be with you♪

113
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,879
(Sometimes I've thought that)

114
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:32,319
(if I ever met someone)

115
00:05:32,639 --> 00:05:33,959
(who truly cared for me,)

116
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,920
(I'd gladly marry him)

117
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,600
(and spend my life by his side,)

118
00:05:40,399 --> 00:05:41,399
(and grow old together.)

119
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
♪Through a thousand twists and turns♪

120
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:47,440
♪I would stay only for you♪

121
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:06,347
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

122
00:06:06,481 --> 00:06:10,094
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

123
00:06:10,329 --> 00:06:12,928
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

124
00:06:12,965 --> 00:06:15,245
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

125
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:19,121
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

126
00:06:19,523 --> 00:06:22,876
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

127
00:06:23,803 --> 00:06:27,316
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

128
00:06:27,816 --> 00:06:30,383
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

129
00:06:30,509 --> 00:06:32,542
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

130
00:06:32,609 --> 00:06:36,386
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

131
00:06:36,736 --> 00:06:41,069
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

132
00:06:41,292 --> 00:06:44,799
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

133
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:47,833
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

134
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:53,514
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

135
00:06:53,554 --> 00:06:56,568
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

136
00:06:56,609 --> 00:07:02,617
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

137
00:07:03,284 --> 00:07:10,239
♪The past has faded away♪

138
00:07:10,239 --> 00:07:14,000
♪The past has faded away♪
